<title>USA: Atlas buys PAL B747-200 as future freighter.</title>
<headline>Atlas buys PAL B747-200 as future freighter.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlas Air said it has bought a General Electric powered Boeing 747-200 all passenger aircraft now flying on lease for Philippine Airlines.</p>
<p>Neither the former owner of the aircraft nor the purchase price was disclosed.</p>
<p>The plane was acquired for future conversion to freighter configuration, said Atlas.</p>
<p>Atlas, the world's largest operator of 747-200 freighters, said that as part of the purchase, it has assumed the balance of the Philippine Air lease. It also will receive a spare engine.</p>
<p>-Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
